.TH PYGTK-POSTING 1 "September 2026" "PyGtk Posting" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pygtk-posting \- accounting and business management for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pygtk-posting
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pygtk-posting
starts PyGtk Posting, an open source accounting and business management
system built with Gtk and backed by PostgreSQL. It covers invoicing,
purchase orders, inventory, manufacturing, payroll, time tracking and
reporting, and prints documents from LibreOffice (.odt) and HTML
templates, including Zebra (ZPL) product labels.
.PP
The program takes no options. It connects to the PostgreSQL server
recorded in its settings file; when that fails, or on the first run, it
opens the database settings window instead so the server can be chosen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/posting/local_settings
Connection details and per-user settings (an SQLite database).
.TP
.I ~/.config/posting/templates/
Working copies of the document templates, seeded from
.I /usr/share/pygtk_posting/templates/
on the first run. Edit these to customise printed documents.
.TP
.I ~/.config/posting/modules/
Working copies of the optional modules, seeded from
.IR /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/pygtk_posting/modules/ .
.TP
.I ~/.config/posting/logs/
One log file per session.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Help menu inside the program, and
.UR https://github.com/benreu/PyGtk-Posting
the project page
.UE .
